Third-party code
----------------
The ward binary statically links third-party Go modules and the Go standard
library. Their licence texts, NOTICE and PATENTS files ship in the
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/ directory of each binary release archive.

Third-party data
----------------
pkg/detect/ngrams.bin and the benign records (label "benign-majestic") of
testdata/eval/lexical-v1.jsonl are derived from the Majestic Million
(https://majestic.com/reports/majestic-million), (c) Majestic-12 Ltd,
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Unported License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/). The data was modified:
ngrams.bin holds quantised character-trigram statistics (no domain names);
the eval fixture is a 1-in-10 sample of ranks 1-20,000. Snapshot hash and regeneration steps: pkg/detect/NOTICE and
testdata/eval/NOTICE.
